Report why a worksheet ended, and bound what a cell reference can cost.

xlsxioread_sheet_next_row() returns 0 at the end of a worksheet and on any
error alike, and under patch 0001 an inflate failure ends the stream as if it
were complete. A damaged or truncated worksheet therefore read as the rows
before the damage, with nothing to say so. This patch keeps the first reason
a worksheet stopped early and adds xlsxioread_sheet_finish(), which the
reader calls once next_row() has returned 0:

  XLSXIOREAD_SHEET_ERROR_XML           Expat reported a parse error. It is
                                       recorded when it happens, because the
                                       next XML_ResumeParser() overwrites it.
  XLSXIOREAD_SHEET_ERROR_RANGE         a cell reference past XFD1048576.
                                       get_col_nr() and get_row_nr() now
                                       saturate one past the grid, so a long
                                       reference cannot wrap size_t, and the
                                       cell is refused before the padding
                                       loops walk towards it -- one cell at
                                       A99999999999 used to keep the reader
                                       busy for minutes.
  XLSXIOREAD_SHEET_ERROR_SHAREDSTRING  a t="s" index that is not a number, is
                                       negative, or is past the table. It
                                       used to read as a blank cell.
  XLSXIOREAD_SHEET_ERROR_ZIP           under USE_MINIZ, finish closes the
                                       archive member, which is where miniz
                                       checks its size and CRC-32.
  XLSXIOREAD_SHEET_ERROR_MISSING       the worksheet's part was never found,
                                       which used to read as an empty sheet.

It also corrects two predicates patch 0003 added to classify number formats:

  numfmt_code_is_date() treated any bracket containing h, m or s as elapsed
  time. Locale tags such as [$$-en-US], which Excel writes for US dollars,
  and colours such as [Magenta] and [White] contain those letters, so
  currency amounts read as dates. A bracket is now elapsed time only when it
  holds one of h, m or s, repeated, and nothing else.

  numfmt_builtin_is_date() missed the East Asian built-in date formats
  (27-36, 50-58) and the Thai ones (71-81), which Excel writes without a
  format code.

Written for zuxlsx. None of it is upstream.

